a couple of months ago we asked  Americans who they trusted to keep their  personal information private and we  found that more Americans trusted  government agencies like the NSA and the  IRS than private companies like Facebook  and Google however in this poll we took  it a step further instead of just asking  about protecting their personal  information we wanted we wanted to know  who they were most concerned about  violating their personal information and  as it turns out a majority are more  concerned about government agencies like  the IRS and the NSA violating them than  they are private companies like Facebook  and Google and what this tells us is  that Americans make a distinction  between government collection of  personal data and private companies  collecting personal data because they  understand that private companies are  using this information to sell them  things and the government is using this  information to spy on them and they  think the government spying on them is  worse  you
 

